{"full":"hf:vllm-sr/decision-studio","spaceId":"vllm-sr/decision-studio","name":"Decision Studio","source":"huggingface","description":"One pass. Many decisions. Try Decision models.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":19,"created":"2025-08-22T17:33:50.000Z","updated":"2026-10-04T06:52:58.000Z","license":"mit","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://vllm-sr-decision-studio.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/vllm-sr/decision-studio","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T17:10:45.644Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T17:10:45.644Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T17:10:45.644Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🎲","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Ask many Choice, Noul and Score questions about one input and read every probability. Decision 2.0 models answer all questions about the same input together in one forward pass; Decision 1.0 stays available beside them for comparison. Route a prompt before calling an LLM, compare a batch of contexts with shared questions, or ask several related questions about one case, with nine LLM-routing scenarios plus model-specific English scenarios.","Decision 2.0 collection · Decision 1.0 collection","The deployed service also includes a server-authoritative Tetris Race playground. It can compare any two configured Decision models, Jev Cloud, or a SystemOne upstream without exposing provider credentials to the browser. Both runners receive the same seeded piece sequence but keep independent boards, requests, actions, timing, and traces."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/vllm-sr/decision-studio/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e4e469b3c056a826db5ef9db757a60deaf7c8bb84bdccec7969a93ad48b82b87","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T17:10:45.702Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T17:10:45.702Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Ask many Choice, Noul and Score questions about one